The assumptions predicates, generated facts, query pipeline, handlers and
refinement rules in crates/symox-core/src/ask follow SymPy 1.14.

The polynomial helpers in python/symox/polys/polyfuncs.py, specialpolys.py,
orthopolys.py, partfrac.py, dispersion.py, monomials.py, orderings.py and
polytools.py, the Poly method wrappers in python/symox/polys/_poly_methods.py
(revert, sqf_norm, nth_power_roots_poly and related structural methods) and
the sparse exponent transforms and the cyclotomic recognition
(dup_cyclotomic_p) in crates/symox-core/src/poly/structure.rs, the orthogonal
polynomial recurrences in crates/symox-core/src/poly/orthopolys.rs, the
Bronstein full partial fraction decomposition in
crates/symox-core/src/poly/partfrac.rs and the dispersion set in
crates/symox-core/src/poly/dispersion.rs follow the corresponding SymPy
algorithms and recurrences.

The symbolic product evaluation and Product/Sum convergence tests in
crates/symox-core/src/products.rs and the recurrence solvers in
crates/symox-core/src/recurr.rs (Abramov's rsolve_poly and rsolve_ratio,
Petkovsek's rsolve_hyper, casoratian and the rsolve driver) follow the
algorithms and case analysis of SymPy's sympy/concrete/products.py,
sympy/concrete/summations.py and sympy/solvers/recurr.py.

The deterministic LLL update order and float-to-rational conversion in
crates/symox-core/src/matrix/lll.rs follow the corresponding SymPy routines.
The auxiliary matrix kernels in crates/symox-core/src/matrix/auxiliary.rs and
python/symox/_matrix_aux.py (Berkowitz vectors, fraction-free and simple LU,
permanent, inverse_BLOCK, Householder Hessenberg and bidiagonal reductions,
dual, get_diag_blocks, irregular, orthogonalize, casoratian, randMatrix,
banded, liupc and the Expr.equals heuristics used by Matrix.equals) are ports
of the corresponding SymPy routines.
